# What Vercel uploads. Everything not listed here is the published surface.
#
# The site is one self-contained page. The kit is spliced into index.html at
# build time and the data files are rendered into it at build time, so at
# runtime the page fetches nothing: a render under the production headers makes
# exactly one request, for the document itself. Every path below is therefore
# source, not surface, and was being deployed only as a side effect of
# deploying the repository.
#
# This is not cosmetic. kit/demo.html was reachable, linked by nothing, refused
# by the site's own content security policy, and rendering seven per-seat
# percentages beside the word MEASURED. A page nobody needs cannot be broken
# and cannot be misread.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because the deployment needs them:
#   index.html og-image.png robots.txt sitemap.xml   the published surface
#   vercel.json                                      routing and headers
#   middleware.js package.json package-lock.json     the edge middleware build

# The drawing kit: spliced inline at build time, plus its demo page and its
# reference screenshots. 3.4 MB of source that no visitor requests.
kit/

# Build and validation helpers. They run before a commit, never in a request.
tools/

# Content sources rendered into the page at build time.
data/

# Developer documentation. Describes internals and links into kit/.
docs/
README.md

# A reproducible writeup of three bypasses in a live control. All three are
# closed, so this is not urgent, but a portfolio has no reason to publish it.
# It stays in the repository, where the audit record belongs.
SECURITY_REPORT.md

# Repository metadata with no meaning to a browser.
.gitattributes
.gitignore
